  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COD21001 R&#xe9;serve Portefeuille RDC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Portefeuille RDC The COD21001 Reserve Portefeuille RDC project, located in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) within the unspecified sector (99810), is a collaboration between Enabel and the Government of DRC. The project&apos;s primary focus is on Reserve UGA 23-27, with an expected duration from 2024 to 2028. The project aims to implement interventions in the agricultural sector, funded by the Direction Generale de la Cooperation au Developpement (DGD). It involves various institutions and organizations such as the Government Provincial, Entite Territoriale Decentralisee (ETD), Assemblee Provinciale, Services Techniques Decentralises, and several non-governmental organizations like CARITAS, CAP CONGO, RACOJ, and privates like FEC. The project&apos;s scope includes institutions like INERA (Institut National d&#x2019;Etudes et Recherches Agronomiques), ISEA (Institut Superieur d&#x2019;Etudes Agronomiques), ITA (Institut Technique Agricole), and ITAPEL (Inspection Territorial de l&apos;Agriculture, Peche et Elevage). The project also involves local organizations such as Regroupement des Acteurs Locaux pour le Developpement du Kasai-Oriental (RADELKOR) and Programmes Specifiques. But it is clear that it aims to contribute to the agricultural sector in the Lomami province of DRC. Further details about the project&apos;s specific interventions, rationale, and expected outcomes can be found in the annual report of Enabel for the period April 2023 to March 2024.</narrative>
  </description>
